WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.771
Your coding agent can open a pull request in a few minutes.

2
00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:10.198
Then somebody has to review it, merge it and ship it. Usually, that's you.

3
00:00:10.198 --> 00:00:13.850
Orbi runs the whole line, from the Issue to the release.

4
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:18.557
You label a GitHub Issue ai-ready. That's the handoff.

5
00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:24.464
Orbi writes the code on its own branch, runs the tests and opens the PR.

6
00:00:24.464 --> 00:00:29.406
Then a second session reviews it against the Issue's acceptance criteria.

7
00:00:29.406 --> 00:00:36.334
On this delivery, it rejected the first attempt. Orbi fixed the finding and tested again.

8
00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:43.298
Only the reviewed commit can merge. If something doesn't add up, Orbi stops and tells you why.

9
00:00:43.298 --> 00:00:49.664
When the milestone is done, it tags a release, with every Issue and PR in the notes.

10
00:00:49.664 --> 00:00:55.038
Every step is a comment on GitHub. The repository is the record.

11
00:00:55.038 --> 00:01:01.560
We build Orbi with Orbi: 69 releases in its first month, all of it public.

12
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:07.527
Self-host it for free, or start on Orbi Cloud. Your first three deliveries are free.

13
00:01:07.527 --> 00:01:10.962
File an Issue. Get a release.
